{"name":"Charlie Horse","hex":"#948263","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"charlie horse","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of charley horse."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/charlie_horse"}],"entries":[{"title":"Charlie Horse","blocks":[{"text":"Charlie Horse is a band based in Sydney, Australia. The group formed in 2010, and as of 2013 had released two albums, I Hope I'm Not A Monster in 2012 on Laughing Outlaw Records and Strange Passengers on Plus One Records in 2013. They released an EP in 2011 titled I Killed My Mind and three singles with accompanying film clips, \"I Killed My Mind\", \"Dead Roses\", and \"Deep Water\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlie_Horse","wikidata":"Q19872128"},{"title":"Charley horse","blocks":[{"text":"Charley horse is a term that typically refers to a muscle cramp, stiffness, or contusion. Generally it is used for the thigh, calf, or foot, or more rarely, the arm. In British English the term may be used interchangeably with leg cramp, dead leg or thigh contusion."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charley_horse","wikidata":"Q638011"},{"title":"Horse","blocks":[{"text":"The horse is a domesticated, one-toed, hoofed mammal. It belongs to the taxonomic family Equidae and is one of two extant subspecies of Equus ferus. The horse has evolved over the past 45 to 55 million years from a small multi-toed creature, Eohippus, into the large single-toed animal of today, originally in North America. Humans began domesticating horses around 4000 BCE in Central Asia, primarily associated with the Botai culture; their domestication is believed to have been widespread by 3000 BCE. However, contemporary genetic evidence indicates that modern domesticated breeds do not descend from this lineage, instead pointing to the Western Eurasian steppes in the lower Volga-Don region as the homeland of modern domestic horses. The modern horse breed replaced the local populations through their rapid expansion across Eurasia from 2000 BCE. Horses in the subspecies caballus are domesticated, although some domesticated populations live in the wild as feral horses. These feral populations are not true wild horses, which are horses that have never been domesticated. There is an extensive, specialized vocabulary used to describe equine-related concepts, covering everything from anatomy to life stages, size, colors, markings, breeds, locomotion, and behavior."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Nokota_Horses_cropped.jpg/330px-Nokota_Horses_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horse","wikidata":"Q726"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Points_of_a_horse.jpg/500px-Points_of_a_horse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Points_of_a_horse.jpg/500px-Points_of_a_horse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"External anatomy of a horse[3][4]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APoints_of_a_horse.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Horse-and-pony.jpg/500px-Horse-and-pony.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Horse-and-pony.jpg/1280px-Horse-and-pony.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Horse-and-pony.jpg/500px-Horse-and-pony.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Size varies greatly among horse breeds, as with this full-sized horse and small pony.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHorse-and-pony.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/c